      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T18:11:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Because ignoreIds is included in Key.equals() and Key.hashCode(), these entries are strictly isolated and will not collide with or pollute regular unignored cache keys,\n\nWe don\u0027t use the hash of the key as \"cache key\". We format the cache key from the fields and right now it doesn\u0027t include the ignore ids. \n\nI *think* this wouldnt break anything because we cannot set the ignored ids in our BlameCache implementation (we would hit the UnsupportedOperation in the default implementation). But if for some reason we default to this implementation somewhere, we would be in trouble.\n\nAdding the ignoreIds to the key before adding everything else, would give us a change to update our implementation without writing wrong keys by accident.\n\n\u003e with standard LRU eviction reclaiming older entries as commits advance.\n\nThis interface doesn\u0027t require implementations to have LRU ;)",
      "parentUuid": "ad27218e_78a09a8b",
      "revId": "196c02cbd1630da4ddc82c2007c45bd9a7458995",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
